(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[26 1 "// _ssl's SSL objects (queue 209): _SSLSocket over a socket or two MemoryBIOs, SSLSession and MemoryBIO."] [27 1 "//"] [28 1 "// The pipe adapter. Go's tls.Conn wants a net.Conn it may block on; OpenSSL's callers (ssl.py over a"] [29 1 "// non-blocking socket, asyncio's SSLProtocol over MemoryBIOs) want SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ and an operation"] [30 1 "// resumed by the next call. So each SSL object runs its tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own (the engine) over"] [31 1 "// an in-memory transport: the engine's Read takes what the Python side fed it and, when there is nothing,"] [32 1 "// tells the Python side it wants input and waits; its Write appends to the bytes to send. Control alternates"] [33 1 "// strictly (the Python thread waits on the engine's event with the GIL released, the engine waits on the"] [34 1 "// Python side's resume), so the engine touches no Python object and the transport's buffers have one owner at"] [35 1 "// a time. The Python side feeds the engine one TLS record at a time (its header, then its length), never"] [36 1 "// more, so after an unwrap the plain bytes behind close_notify stay in the socket as with OpenSSL. A callback"] [37 1 "// the engine needs (the SNI callback) runs on the Python thread with the GIL. Writes and close_notify, which"] [38 1 "// never wait for input, are made on the Python thread directly once the handshake is done (tls.Conn's write"] [39 1 "// side is independent of its read side)."] [62 1 "// sslEngine is the goroutine side: the tls.Conn and its transport's buffers."] [74 2 "// alert is the description the SNI callback asked for (OpenSSL's *al), 0 when none: Go's server sends"] [75 2 "// internal_error when GetConfigForClient fails, so the transport puts this description in that alert record"] [76 2 "// (still in the clear: nothing is encrypted before the server's hello)"] [118 1 "// call runs f on the Python thread (from the engine)."] [139 1 "// pySSLSocket is an SSL object (PySSLSocket)."] [143 24 "// nil: over MemoryBIOs"] [163 24 "// the incoming record being fed, for the message callback"] [164 24 "// the bytes at the head of the engine's output already traced (a socket's unsent rest)"] [165 24 "// the version the message callback reports: the server hello's, once seen"] [175 1 "// sslVerifyError is a certificate verification failure: OpenSSL's code and message."] [183 1 "// ---- the session cache of one connection: the session given, the session received ----"] [198 2 "// the session's id: its state's digest, so a resumed session renewed by the server keeps it (OpenSSL keeps"] [199 2 "// the session id across a resumption)"] [216 1 "// ---- the configuration ----"] [255 1 "// serverConfig is GetConfigForClient: the SNI callback run on the Python thread (it may switch the socket's"] [256 1 "// context), the configuration made of the context then in force, ALPN without a protocol in common answered"] [257 1 "// with none (CPython's callback returns SSL_TLSEXT_ERR_NOACK; Go's server would refuse the handshake)."] [269 19 "// replaced since the handshake looked"] [274 5 "// _servername_callback: PyErr_FormatUnraisable, then SSL_AD_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE"] [280 5 "// an integer is the alert's description; anything else SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR, with the unraisable"] [326 1 "// verify is _ssl's verification (OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert with the context's store, then X509_check_host when"] [327 1 "// check_hostname): the codes of OpenSSL's x509_vfy.h."] [353 62 "// a fallback root's constraint"] [389 30 "// VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF (and _CHAIN, which checks the leaf too)"] [413 31 "// VERIFY_X509_STRICT: RFC 5280's AKI on a certificate not self-issued"] [432 1 "// sslCheckHost is X509_check_host / X509_check_ip_asc: 0 when the certificate names host, else 62 (or 64 for an"] [433 1 "// address). The subject's common name is looked at only without a DNS name and without"] [434 1 "// HOSTFLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT; a wildcard only as the whole leftmost label, over one label, with at least two"] [435 1 "// labels after it."] [471 1 "// ---- errors ----"] [473 1 "// sslReasons are OpenSSL's reasons of the alerts a peer sends, by alert number."] [487 1 "// sslGoReasons are OpenSSL's reasons for Go's own handshake errors, by the start of their text."] [502 1 "// sslReasonText is ERR_reason_error_string's form of a reason: lower case, words apart."] [520 1 "// raiseErr is PySSL_SetError for an operation's Go error: the exception CPython's _ssl raises for what OpenSSL"] [521 1 "// would have reported."] [564 1 "// ---- the transport's two ends on the Python side ----"] [581 1 "// need is how much the record being fed still needs: its header's rest, then its body's."] [591 74 "// from a record's start"] [600 16 "// not a TLS record: the engine refuses its header"] [616 1 "// ---- the message callback (_PySSL_msg_callback) ----"] [617 1 "//"] [618 1 "// OpenSSL calls it from its record layer with each record's header and each message in the clear. The port sees"] [619 1 "// the records on the wire, where the transport carries them: each record's header (SSL3_RT_HEADER), and the"] [620 1 "// messages of the records still in the clear (the handshake's messages up to the change of keys, change cipher"] [621 1 "// spec, alerts). A record sent or received under the keys is seen by its header alone: Go's tls.Conn keeps its"] [622 1 "// keys, so TLS 1.2's Finished and TLS 1.3's encrypted handshake (and SSL3_RT_INNER_CONTENT_TYPE) are not reported."] [624 1 "// sslMsgTrace is one direction's state: whether its records are under the keys, a handshake message's bytes so far."] [632 1 "// traceIn reports the incoming record just fed (flush reports the outgoing ones)."] [653 26 "// before the server hello: the highest version the context allows, as OpenSSL's"] [658 21 "// change cipher spec is in the clear (TLS 1.3's too, middlebox compatibility's)"] [659 4 "// SSL3_MT_CHANGE_CIPHER_SPEC; OpenSSL 3.5 reports a received one under TLS 1.3 only (TLS 1.2's"] [660 4 "// record layer consumes it unreported)"] [684 22 "// the server hello names the version"] [691 49 "// the rest of the handshake is under the keys"] [700 1 "// sslHelloVersion is a server hello's version: its supported_versions extension's, else its legacy version."] [752 1 "// takeCbErr is PySSL_ChainExceptions after an operation that succeeded: a callback's exception is raised."] [759 1 "// fill feeds the engine the next bytes of the current record: false when they are not there yet (a"] [760 1 "// non-blocking socket, an empty incoming BIO)."] [818 1 "// flush sends what the engine wrote: into the outgoing BIO, or to the socket (a non-blocking one's rest kept,"] [819 1 "// SSLWantWriteError)."] [881 1 "// step hands control to the engine, starting op (nil: resuming it), until it waits for input or is done; the"] [882 1 "// callbacks it asks for run here."] [903 1 "// drive runs an engine operation (resuming the one in flight first) to its end: OpenSSL's loop of SSL_do_handshake"] [904 1 "// or SSL_read with the socket's waits; SSLWantReadError when its input is not there yet."] [969 1 "// ---- the methods ----"] [983 2 "// close_notify received: SSL_read's zero return is 0 bytes while it is the only shutdown seen"] [984 2 "// (SSL_RECEIVED_SHUTDOWN), SSLZeroReturnError once this side sent its own"] [1091 27 "// the peer closed the transport: SSL_shutdown's second call gives up"] [1106 1 "// ---- wrap ----"] [1221 1 "// ---- SSLSession ----"] [1232 1 "// ---- MemoryBIO ----"] [1399 21 "// SSL_get_client_ciphers is a server's"] [1486 4 "// a resumed session keeps its id and time (a ticket the server renewed only replaces its state)"] [1497 30 "// OpenSSL's session of a connection that got no ticket (yet)"] [1508 2 "// SSLSession"] [1530 2 "// MemoryBIO"] [1580 1 "// ---- PKCS #8 encryption (PBES2 with PBKDF2, RFC 8018), which Go's x509 does not read ----"] [1678 1 "// sslTimeout is the TimeoutError of an operation past the socket's timeout (the handshake's message with"] [1679 1 "// ERRSTR's prefix, as _ssl.c has it)."] [1687 1 "// sslPBKDF2 is RFC 8018's PBKDF2 with HMAC over prf (crypto/pbkdf2's Key is generic, which goi's table does not"] [1688 1 "// call)."] [1714 1 "// sslDistrustedSPKI are the SHA-256 digests of the public keys _ssl refuses in any chain (Modules/_ssl/"] [1715 1 "// distrusted_spki.h, gh-160040: the compromised eMudhra intermediates)."] [1738 1 "// afterHandshake is what OpenSSL keeps of a finished handshake: the context's session statistics, and the"] [1739 1 "// anchor its by-hash lookup loaded from a capath directory, now in the store (get_ca_certs lists it)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[90 25] [103 19] [202 39] [203 26] [210 24] [243 38] [282 29] [313 22] [420 38] [421 63] [437 28] [544 29] [575 19] [685 34] [714 34] [908 42] [961 43] [1019 25] [1027 57] [1035 28] [1039 19] [1042 32] [1045 56] [1051 25] [1058 27] [1065 19] [1073 34] [1097 59] [1150 44] [1166 31] [1196 31] [1265 28] [1271 33] [1332 33] [1548 33] [1693 16] [1693 35] [1699 13] [1699 23] [1703 14] [1703 21] [1712 54] [1754 25]] :go/trails [[484 127] [499 76] [1724 68]]} (go/file "builtins_ssl_conn.go" :imports [


